# What `vercel deploy` must not upload.
#
# .gitignore is NOT consulted for deploy uploads — backend.zip is listed there
# and was still sent, failing the deploy on Vercel's 100 MB limit. Because a
# .vercelignore is used *instead of* .gitignore, this file has to repeat
# everything .gitignore excluded rather than only adding to it. In particular
# .env* must stay listed: those files hold DATABASE_URL and the OpenRouter key,
# and dropping the line would start shipping them into the deployment source.

# --- Local archive (~283 MB — the reason this file exists) ---------------
/backend.zip

# --- Node / Next.js ------------------------------------------------------
node_modules
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
.vercel

# --- Python backend (deploys to Railway, never built or served by Vercel) -
# Excluded wholesale now that it is a separately deployed service: Vercel has
# no use for it and uploading it only slows every deploy. Railway builds this
# directory from the same repo with Root Directory = backend.
backend/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# --- SQL assets (applied to Railway Postgres by db/bootstrap_remote.py) --
# The Next.js app creates its own table via ensureSchema(); these dumps are
# for the FastAPI schema and are megabytes of snapshot data.
db/backups/
db/live_snapshot.sql

# --- Secrets & local env -------------------------------------------------
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem

# --- Runtime artifacts ---------------------------------------------------
captures/
*.log

# --- OS / editor ---------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
